The '''Mimban Campaign''', also known as the '''Battle of Mimban''' or '''Occupation of Mimban''', was a [[planet]]ary war between the [[Galactic Empire]] and [[Mimbanese Liberation Army]] in [[10 BBY]] during the early [[Standard year|years]] of the [[Imperial Era]] on the [[swamp]] world of [[Mimban]] in an effort to secure the planet's vital resources while establishing a regime loyal to the Empire. The [[224th Imperial Armored Division]] engaged the Mimbanese Liberation Army, with the latter eager to drive the Imperials from their [[homeworld]] at all costs. The campaign saw the deployment of numerous [[Imperial swamp trooper]]s and [[wet-weather gear stormtrooper]]s, with the Imperial [[Imperial Army|ground forces]] making use of [[trench warfare]] against the native [[Mimbanese]].

==Prelude==
===Historical background===
{{Quote|Like Ryloth, Mimban had seen heavy combat during the Clone Wars with the Mimbanese Liberation Army undertaking battles against the invading Separatists. Mimban also had considerable natural resources that had first made it a target for the Separatists, and then the Empire. The plentiful deposits of hyperbarides&mdash;crucial components of turbolaser production&mdash;made the planet a highly tempting target, but the Liberation Army were no more willing to allow the Empire to conquer them than they had been the Separatists.|Beaumont Kin, ''The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire''|<ref name="Rise and Fall" />}}
The planet [[Mimban]] was a backwater [[Expansion Region]] that was home to several species including the [[Mimbanese]]. The planet was rich in [[hyperbaride]] minerals, making it the target of energy [[mining]] interests and various governments including the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], the [[Galactic Republic]], and the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="TOG" /> The Confederacy's mining devastated the world's environment.<ref name="Bust Collection 51">{{BustCollectionCite|51|Character}}</ref>

[[File:BattleOfMimban-501PlusOne.jpg|thumb|left|300px|Mimban was targeted by various galactic powers due to its mineral resources]]
During the [[Clone Wars]], Mimban was invaded by the [[Confederacy military]]. The indigenous [[Mimbanese Liberation Army]] [[Battle of Mimban|resisted]] the Separatist forces with aid from the [[Galactic Republic]]. Members of the [[Grand Army of the Republic]]'s [[224th Imperial Armored Division|224th Division]], known as the mud-jumpers, fought alongside the Mimbanese, promising the species freedom once the Separatists were defeated.<ref name="TOG" /> Following the transformation of the Republic into the Galactic Empire in [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> the Empire sought to exploit Mimban for its mineral resources in order to fuel the Imperial war machine<ref name="TOG" /> despite the ecological devastation its mining caused,<ref name="2022 Calendar" /> like that of the Confederacy before it.<ref name="Bust Collection 51" /> [[Stacks]],<ref name="GE-EotE2">[[Galaxy's Edge – Echoes of the Empire 2|''Galaxy's Edge – Echoes of the Empire'' 2]]</ref> a clone trooper who went on to serve the Empire as a stormtrooper,<ref name="Andor Props">{{SW|url=news/disneyland-galaxys-edge-update-details|text=''Andor'' Props and Other New Updates to See Inside ''Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge'' at Disneyland}}</ref> took part in<ref name="GE-EotE2" /> the Imperial operations<ref name="MimbanBattle">{{Bluesky|ethansacks.bsky.social|post/3mmuae2p3i22l|[[Ethan Sacks]]|date=2026-05-27|quote=No worries. I answer questions when I can. In this case, to your original question, Stacks would have fought for the Empire in the beginning. So he's referring to the Imperial campaign.}} {{c|In response to: "Out of curiosity @ethansacks.bsky.social, which was your intention for the battle of Mimban that Stacks fought in? The Clone Wars battle or the Imperial Era campaign, or even both since some of the same units bled over?" and and "shooting an apology over to @ethansacks.bsky.social for asking this before the full release, realize now you might prefer to have these questions after the formal release not after previews, heh, sorry about that boss"}}</ref> on Mimban.<ref name="GE-EotE2" />

===Imperial entanglements and politics===
{{Quote|As previously noted, there remain strong suggestions that the Empire aimed to drag the campaign out for as long as possible to force further military requisition bills through the Senate. To achieve this, attacks on civilian Mimbanese targets were widespread in order to motivate the population to continue to fight a perpetually losing battle, rather than surrender.|Beaumont Kin, ''The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire|<ref name="Rise and Fall" />}}
The Empire's activity on Mimban had started conflict by the time [[Cassian Jeron Andor]] was sixteen years old. Andor was conscripted into the armed forces during his time in prison. He was immediately deployed to Mimban and participated in six months of fighting, although technically he was only the unit's cook. Andor himself, however, would claim he saw active combat.<ref name="Episode 4">{{Andor|Aldhani (episode)}}</ref> Under the orders of [[Grand Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]], [[Moff]] [[Bin Essada]] of the [[Circarpous sector]] sought to procure the abundant natural resources that existed on the swampy world. The Imperials encountered resistance from their former Mimbanese allies<ref name="TOG" /> as they attempted to occupy Mimban.<ref name="Occupation">{{Topps|set=2020 Topps Star Wars Holocron Series|subset=The Adventures of Han Solo|cardname=Occupation of Mimban}}</ref> Where possible, Imperial forces attempted to wipe out portions of the Mimbanese population. These attacks on the civilian population proved to be widespread, which inspired the Mimbanese to continue their ultimately-doomed resistance against the Empire.<ref name="Rise and Fall" />

[[File:Mudtroopers_on_Mimban.png|thumb|right|300px|The Mimban Campaign was a prolonged, torturous battle for the Imperial Army.]]
The Mimban Campaign dragged on for a considerable period of time. However, the later historian [[Beaumont Kin]] would theorize in his book ''[[The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]'' that creating such a prolonged conflict had been part of the intention behind the Mimban Campaign in the first place; while the Empire no doubt wanted the planet's resources, Kin pointed out that the Empire had been able to use the campaign as on-the-ground training for its soldiers and as a justification for the [[Imperial Senate]] to approve additional military funding. While the overall Empire was, in theory, at peace, Imperial officials were able to claim the reason the Mimban Campaign was taking so long was a lack of resources. In reality, Kin theorized that [[General]] [[Ire Falk]]&mdash;the commander of the Mimban invasion&mdash;had been ordered to prolong the battle for as long as possible as a smokescreen for these legislative efforts. The widespread assault on Mimbanese civilians was launched as part of this effort, inspiring the locals to not surrender so as to continue the torturous battle. Further, images of the war-torn Mimban were useful in Imperial [[propaganda]], which used the besieged planet as a backdrop for reporters who painted the image of the [[Imperial Military]] holding back chaos and devastation.<ref name="Rise and Fall" />

==The campaign==
===Skirmish in the trenches===
{{Quote|Your Empire needs you. Troopers, forward!|Staz to his troops shortly before being killed in an explosion|<ref name="Solo" />}}
[[File:Solo_trailer_AT-DT.png|thumb|left|300px|Imperial forces deployed to a frontline of the Mimban Campaign]]
Around [[10 BBY]], the 224th Imperial Armored Division, consisting of both [[Imperial Army]] [[Imperial swamp trooper]]s and [[wet-weather gear stormtrooper]]s, was deployed to Mimban. The 224th Armored Division established a temporary headquarters called [[Imperial Forward Field Operations]] inside the disputed wilderness zone. The Division was locked into [[trench warfare]] against the Mimbanese Liberation Army, which used guerrilla tactics including improvised mines, tripwires, and catapults against Imperial forces and vehicles.<ref name="TOG" />

In one of the bloodiest battles of the campaign,<ref name="Bust Collection 51" /> known simply as the [[battle on Mimban]],<ref name="Solo Meet the Crew">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story: Meet the Crew]]''</ref> [[Major]] [[Staz]] led a group of Swamp troopers including [[Corporal]] [[Han Solo]] in a ground assault to capture a ridge from the Mimbanese. The Mimbanese fired explosives which killed Major Staz. Han and several soldiers<ref name="Solo" /> including Corporal [[Danith Nodar]], [[Private]] [[Collum Woslo]], Corporal [[Sharlu Greslin]], Corporal [[Wesger Odry]], Medic [[Gorji Sandem]], Private [[Bokret Humphreys]], Specialist [[Gillen Finders]], Sergeant [[Mattiso Trodu]], and Corporal [[Chakobi Sanwright]]<ref name="TOG" /> regrouped in a trench under the command of "[[Captain]]" [[Tobias Beckett]], the last senior officer in the group. Beckett led the Swamp troopers in a successful assault on the ridge.<ref name="Solo" />

===Solo's desertion===
[[File:BeckettHanMimban-Solo.jpg|thumb|right|350px|Corporal Han Solo encountered the smuggler Tobias Beckett during the Mimban Campaign, initiating the young Corellian's life of crime.]]
Following the skirmish, [[Lieutenant]] [[Alayus Bolandin]] told Solo and his comrades that they would be departing within three [[Standard hour|hours]] to the [[Southern Marshlands]]. He also requested volunteers for an advance party. When Solo questioned what the Empire was doing to Mimban and suggested that the Imperials were the aggressors, Bolandin regarded Solo as a troublemaker.<ref name="Solo" />

During a break in the fighting, Solo encountered "Captain" Beckett and his [[Beckett's gang|gang]] associates [[Val]] and [[Rio Durant]], whom he ascertained were smugglers dressed in stolen Imperial uniforms. The criminals were planning to commandeer a [[Y-45 armored transport hauler]]. Recognizing this as an opportunity to leave behind his life as a mere grunt, Solo initially attempted to persuade Beckett into allowing him into the group, offering his services as a pilot.<ref name="Solo" />

[[File:Hairy_and_the_Boy.jpg|thumb|left|300px|Solo meets Chewbacca]]
When Beckett and his gang rebuffed Solo, he threatened to expose them as infiltrators. However, Beckett turned the tables on Solo by convincing Lieutenant Bolandin that they had caught Solo trying to [[Desertion|desert]] the Imperial Army. Seeking to rid the unit of a troublemaker, Bolandin threw Solo into a pit to be devoured by "the beast," a [[Wookiee]] called [[Chewbacca]].<ref name="Solo" /> Chewbacca had been betrayed by a bounty hunter who handed him over to Imperial forces on Mimban.<ref name="TOG" />

While Chewbacca was initially hostile to Solo, Solo managed to use his knowledge of [[Shyriiwook]] and quick wit to convince the Wookiee to help him escape the pen. After breaking out, Solo convinced Chewbacca to come with him to a nearby airfield where Beckett and his gang were preparing to depart on their stolen transport hauler. Impressed by the young man's determination, Beckett allowed both Solo and Chewbacca aboard his stolen AT-hauler.<ref name="Solo" />

===Beilert's ordeal===
[[File:ValanceMimban-TargetVader5.jpg|thumb|right|275px|Beilert Valance leading Swamp troops]]
After suffering injuries that ended his career as a [[Imperial Starfighter Pilot|TIE fighter pilot]],<ref name="Imperial Cadet 5">[[Han Solo - Imperial Cadet 5|''Han Solo - Imperial Cadet'' 5]]</ref> [[Beilert Valance]] was reassigned to the Imperial Army,<ref name="Target Vader 5">[[Target Vader 5|''Target Vader'' 5]]</ref> which he served in as a stormtrooper<ref name="Target Vader 3">[[Target Vader 3|''Target Vader'' 3]]</ref> and also a regular army soldier. Sent into Mimban campaign as a swamp trooper, he and his unit saw action in a trench. Valance attempted to call for air support. When the other soldiers doubted that Imperial reinforcements would come for them, Valance was determined to complete his mission and led his men out of the trench. As a result, Valance suffered life changing injuries including the loss of the left side of his face and his remaining arms and leg. After being discharged from the [[Imperial Military]], Valance became a bounty hunter who worked for the [[Hidden Hand]] crime syndicate and later the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]].<ref name="Target Vader 5" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Mimban campaign first appeared in the [[2018]] film ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''.<ref name="Solo" />

